5.1 Microsoft 365 Licensing

A Microsoft 365 license determines which Microsoft 365 services and features a user is entitled to access according to the assigned plan and service configuration.

Possible services may include:

Exchange Online
Teams
OneDrive
SharePoint
Microsoft 365 applications
Important

A missing feature should not automatically be assumed to be a licensing issue. Other possibilities include authentication, account configuration, service outages, or application problems.

5.2 Shared Mailbox Permissions

A shared mailbox can use different permissions.

Full Access

Allows an authorized user to access and work with the mailbox.

Send As

Allows an authorized user to send a message that appears to come directly from the shared mailbox.

Example:

From: support@company.com
Send on Behalf

Allows a user to send a message on behalf of the shared mailbox.

Example:

John on behalf of support@company.com
Help Desk Scenario

User can open the shared mailbox but cannot send from it.

Possible area to investigate:

Send As permission
Send on Behalf permission
